---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Minted & Gone">
  <div class="shell guide-page about-page">
    <section class="field-hero simple-hero compact-hero about-hero">
      <figure class="hero-botanical hero-page-art" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/about/about-archive-key.png" alt="" loading="eager" /></figure>
      <div class="hero-copy plate-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">About this archive</p>
        <h1>About Minted &amp; Gone</h1>
        <p class="lede">A quiet archive of NFT marketplaces: active, faded, acquired, and gone.</p>
        <p>Minted &amp; Gone preserves marketplace identities, status changes, timeline events, source notes, and archived traces in one place.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="mock-note">The current archive is an early source-reviewed draft. Records are evidence-backed enough for review, but they are not final public-quality certifications.</p>

    <section class="about-section-grid">
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">01</span>
        <h2>What is Minted &amp; Gone?</h2>
        <p>Minted &amp; Gone is a historical registry for NFT marketplaces. It tracks marketplace names, aliases, categories, chain scope, status, shutdowns, acquisitions, community continuations, evidence notes, and what remains after a platform changes or disappears.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">02</span>
        <h2>Why it exists</h2>
        <p>NFT marketplaces can disappear quietly. Domains expire, product pages change, support notices vanish, and old platform histories become hard to reconstruct. This archive keeps those traces reviewable.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">03</span>
        <h2>Who it is for</h2>
        <p>The archive is for collectors, researchers, builders, writers, and curious readers who want to understand how the NFT marketplace landscape changed over time without relying on scattered memories or broken links.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">04</span>
        <h2>What it is not</h2>
        <p>It is not a trading dashboard, marketplace ranking, investment guide, safety certification, legal analysis, full smart-contract audit, or real-time monitoring guarantee.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">05</span>
        <h2>How to read records</h2>
        <p>Records should be read as evidence-backed historical drafts. Confidence levels, evidence notes, archived URLs, and record quality flags explain what is known and what still needs review.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">06</span>
        <h2>How corrections help</h2>
        <p>If you know of a missing marketplace, archived source, official shutdown notice, successor path, or correction, submit it with source links. The archive is designed to improve over time.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="framed-panel definition-card about-cta">
      <p class="eyebrow">Field-guide, not dashboard</p>
      <h2>Designed for reviewable history</h2>
      <p>Minted &amp; Gone intentionally keeps uncertainty visible. The goal is not to smooth every record into a false certainty, but to preserve the current evidence, unresolved flags, and archive trail in a form that can be reviewed and improved.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/methodology/">Read methodology</a><a class="btn" href="/submit/">Submit/correct</a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="framed-panel definition-card about-cta">
      <p class="eyebrow">Help the archive improve</p>
      <h2>Records grow through notes and support</h2>
      <p>Found a missing marketplace or correction? Submit a note. Want to help keep the archive maintained? Support this archive.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/submit/">Submit a note</a><a class="btn" href="/support/">Support this archive</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
